+# Bug Assessment: Inventory is not reserved, restored, or exposed consistently
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+Merchants report that checkout often does not reduce the ordered products' stock, and sometimes reduces another product's stock. Cancellation never restores stock; carts and checkout can exceed inventory; zero-stock products remain available. The requested behavior specifies atomic HTTP 409 rejection for insufficient inventory, exact per-product decrement/restock, idempotent cancellation, forbidden transitions out of canceled, and stock-derived product availability.
+
+## Symptom
+
+Inventory changes are not reliably associated with the ordered product and shortages are logged rather than rejected. Cart edits and checkout can persist quantities beyond stock, cancellation does not return stock, and product responses can report purchasability independently of current quantity.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Create at least two products with distinct stock, add them to a cart, and checkout; compare each product's quantity before and after checkout. [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact fixture/API setup]
+2. Set a cart quantity above product stock through create, PUT, or multi-update, then inspect the response and persisted cart.
+3. Cancel an order, cancel it again, and attempt another status; compare stock after each request.
+4. Fetch `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` for a product with zero stock and for a merchant-unavailable product.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java:191-211` — decrements inventory using `productService.getById(orderProduct.getId())`, logs shortages instead of throwing, and has no cancellation restock/idempotency handling.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java:390-415` — validates checkout quantities but must be coordinated transactionally with order creation and stock mutation.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java:1000-1020, 580-680, 820-930` — cart create, single update, and multi-update mutate and save without a complete atomic stock check.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java:343-468` and `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java:65-175` — endpoint exception handling currently maps inventory failures to generic errors rather than a consistent 409 response.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductPopulator.java:490-510` — product quantity and `canBePurchased` are populated from availability inconsistently; zero stock must force both availability flags false while preserving merchant-unavailable state.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/Order.java` and `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/model/order/orderstatus/OrderStatusHistory.java` — order status/history provide the state needed to make cancellation restock once.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The checkout decrement implementation resolves an order-product identifier as a catalog product identifier and does not fail when inventory is insufficient. Separately, cart mutation methods perform partial in-memory updates before saving and lack a shared atomic stock validator. Order status updates only append history/status, and the product response mapper does not establish stock as the authoritative purchasability condition in all cases.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Centralize stock lookup and validation around the product/variant SKU and the canonical `ProductAvailability.productQuantity`. Add a transactional inventory operation that first validates every cart line, then decrements exactly those lines, and throws a dedicated conflict exception before order creation or persistence on shortage. Apply the same validator to cart creation, single updates, and multi-updates, using a copy/validation pass so multi-update is all-or-none; allow reductions/removals without rejection. Map the conflict exception to HTTP 409.
+
+Make order cancellation transactional and idempotent: when transitioning to `CANCELED`, restore each order line's quantity once, record the transition, and reject any later non-canceled transition with 409. Other transitions do not alter stock. Ensure both anonymous and authenticated checkout use the same transactional path. Set product response `available` and `canBePurchased` from merchant availability plus current positive stock, while retaining merchant-unavailable as an overriding false condition.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/order/facade/OrderFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/order/OrderApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/shoppingCart/ShoppingCartApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductPopulator.java`
+- relevant API/integration tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and service tests under `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+- Checkout with multiple products decrements only each ordered product by its requested quantity.
+- Insufficient checkout returns 409 and leaves both order creation and all stock unchanged.
+- Cart create, single update, and multi-update reject over-stock atomically; zero stock cannot be added, while lowering/removing succeeds.
+- Cancellation restores each line once; repeated cancellation is a no-op and later status changes return 409.
+- Product v2 responses report false flags at zero stock and become purchasable again after restock, unless merchant-unavailable.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Checkout and cancellation need transaction boundaries to prevent partial stock changes and duplicate restoration.
+- Existing orders may lack an explicit inventory-restored marker; order history/status must be used or a compatible persisted marker introduced without breaking existing schemas.
+- Variant availability and multi-region availability need to use the same canonical stock selection as the product endpoint.
+- Existing clients may currently receive 400/503 for inventory errors; the requested 409 behavior is an intentional API change.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: exact integration fixture/database profile for end-to-end API verification]
